 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
 *   **Global Dilation Invalid:** Global dilation cannot be used because the scale index (pyramid level) varies per coefficient, unlike level-by-level projection where the scale is constant for all coefficients in a level [S1].
-*   **Ordering Loss:** Because coefficients are projected by error rather than intensity, voxels are no longer ordered by intensity in the rendering stream. This necessitates using the maximum operator for frame buffer writes, which may cause performance loss compared to alpha-blending or simple overwriting, although the impact is mitigated by the small size of the blended primitives [S1].
